{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure Intent in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent"},{"type":"text","value":" object in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" permits packages or individual skills."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude"}]},{"type":"text","value":" blocks packages or skills after permissions are evaluated."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"skills\": [\n      \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"@acme/*\",\n      \"@tanstack/start#routing\",\n      \"workspace:@scope/internal\"\n    ],\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/router#experimental-*\"]\n  }\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration-inheritance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration inheritance"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inheritance rule"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses the nearest non-null declaration between the current directory and the workspace or project root. A nearer declaration replaces its parent; omitted or null values inherit."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.exclude"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combines arrays from the root through the current directory, then adds excludes passed by the caller."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"intent-skills","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills"},{"type":"text","value":" is a package-source and skill allowlist. A permitted package or skill can:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Appear in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"list"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stale"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolve through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contribute mappings to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"install --map"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"install"},{"type":"text","value":" helps configure permissions on first use. See "},{"type":"link","href":"#existing-projects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing projects"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for how it handles saved or inherited configuration, and "},{"type":"link","href":"./trust-model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trust model"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the trust boundaries."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package selectors permit current and future skills in the package. Exact selectors use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<package>#<skill>"},{"type":"text","value":" and permit only that skill. If both match, the package selector takes precedence. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" is applied afterward and can still block either choice."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"source-entries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source entries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each array entry names one source:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entry"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kind"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@scope/pkg"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pkg"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"npm"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An npm package reachable through the dependency tree, direct or transitive."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@scope/pkg#skill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"npm"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One exact skill in an npm package."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"workspace:@scope/pkg"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A package in the current workspace."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"workspace:@scope/pkg#skill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One exact skill in a workspace package."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@scope/*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"npm"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every discovered npm package whose name matches the pattern."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"workspace:@scope/*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every discovered workspace package whose name matches the pattern."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git:<host>/<repo>#<ref>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"git"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reserved. Not yet supported, and rejected until a future version adds it."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"validation-rules","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation rules"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exact selectors require a non-empty package name and a non-empty skill name without wildcards."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package patterns support "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*"},{"type":"text","value":", including scoped patterns such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/*"},{"type":"text","value":". Patterns cannot be combined with an exact skill selector."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source kinds must match: bare selectors permit npm sources; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"workspace:"},{"type":"text","value":" selectors permit workspace sources."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git:"},{"type":"text","value":" entries are rejected, including entries containing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#"},{"type":"text","value":" for a Git ref."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A malformed entry fails the whole command. Intent reports every bad entry at once."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"special-forms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Special forms"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notice"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Absent:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" no effective "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills"},{"type":"text","value":" key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discovery commands surface every discovered package as migration behavior."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecation notice until you configure permissions."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"skills\": []"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Surfaces no packages."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Info notice on stderr."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wildcard:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"skills\": [\"*\"]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Permits every discovered package across scopes and source kinds, broader than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/*"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Acknowledged-risk notice: unvetted skills may reach your agent."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All policy notices go to stderr. Exclusions still apply to these forms."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"discovery-notices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discovery notices"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Situation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notice"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discovered package is not permitted"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Human output names omitted packages in one notice. Agent sessions receive only hidden package and skill counts."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configured package was not discovered"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reports that the package was not discovered."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configured exact skill is not in its discovered package"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reports that the entry was not discovered."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package was explicitly excluded"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No unlisted-source notice."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"existing-projects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing projects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent list"},{"type":"text","value":" to see which packages the current policy surfaces."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current configuration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent install"},{"type":"text","value":" behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Saved or inherited "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Updates guidance only. Keeps permissions unchanged and does not prompt."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No effective "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Starts interactive permission setup. Non-TTY execution fails without writes."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"First-run setup offers "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable all"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose packages or scopes"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose individual skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":", followed by one confirmation before saving to the nearest owning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":" and installing guidance."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compact rules:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Enable all saves "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"*\""},{"type":"text","value":"; package choices save names such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"@tanstack/ai\""},{"type":"text","value":"; explicit scope choices save patterns such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"@tanstack/*\""},{"type":"text","value":". These rules include future matching skills and packages. Individual choices save exact names such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"@tanstack/ai#skill\""},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional skill review:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" choose "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review individual skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" at confirmation, then pick which selected packages to inspect. Leave the list empty to keep all selected skills. Only those packages open individual skill lists; unchecking a skill covered by a broad rule adds an exclusion. Existing and inherited exclusions stay in force."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changing instructions:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" access choices do not record approval of specific content. Skills can change with dependency updates; update notifications are not available yet."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty selection:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly confirms disabling all skills with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"},{"type":"text","value":". Empty or fully excluded discovery writes nothing, so setup can be retried."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, enabling a scope and unchecking one skill saves:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"skills\": [\"@tanstack/*\"],\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/ai#skill\"]\n  }\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This permits matching npm packages, including future additions, except the excluded skill. Selecting several packages individually never silently expands to a scope rule."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../cli/intent-install#default-install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default install"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for picker controls and cancellation behavior."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"suppressing-notices-temporarily","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suppressing notices temporarily"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--no-notices"},{"type":"text","value":" to suppress non-critical notices on stderr for one run:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"list\",\"--no-notices\"],[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"install\",\"--map\",\"--no-notices\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For CI or wrapper scripts, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"INTENT_NO_NOTICES=1"},{"type":"text","value":" to suppress notices without changing command arguments."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discovery and resolution warnings are separate from policy notices and are not suppressed by these options. The acknowledged-risk notice for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"skills\": [\"*\"]"},{"type":"text","value":" also remains visible when other notices are suppressed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"intent-exclude","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.exclude"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" removes packages or individual skills after the allowlist resolves."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" to manage this list from the CLI:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"exclude\",\"add\",\"@tanstack/router#experimental-*\"],[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"exclude\",\"remove\",\"@tanstack/router#experimental-*\"],[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"exclude\",\"list\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/*devtools*\", \"@tanstack/router#experimental-*\"]\n  }\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"exclusion-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exclusion patterns"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pattern"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Excludes"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@scope/pkg"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The whole package."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@scope/pkg#search-params"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One named skill."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@scope/pkg#experimental-*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Matching skills in one package."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*#experimental-*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Matching skills across packages."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@scope/pkg#*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The whole package, using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#*"},{"type":"text","value":" shortcut."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each segment supports exact names and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*"},{"type":"text","value":" wildcards only. Excludes apply to both npm and workspace sources with matching names, regardless of source kind."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"configuration-inheritance","text":"Configuration inheritance","level":2},{"id":"intent-skills","text":"intent.skills","level":2},{"id":"source-entries","text":"Source entries","level":3},{"id":"validation-rules","text":"Validation rules","level":4},{"id":"special-forms","text":"Special forms","level":3},{"id":"discovery-notices","text":"Discovery notices","level":4},{"id":"existing-projects","text":"Existing projects","level":3},{"id":"suppressing-notices-temporarily","text":"Suppressing notices temporarily","level":3},{"id":"intent-exclude","text":"intent.exclude","level":2},{"id":"exclusion-patterns","text":"Exclusion patterns","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nConfigure Intent in the `intent` object in `package.json`:\n\n- **`skills`** permits packages or individual skills.\n- **`exclude`** blocks packages or skills after permissions are evaluated.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"skills\": [\n      \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"@acme/*\",\n      \"@tanstack/start#routing\",\n      \"workspace:@scope/internal\"\n    ],\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/router#experimental-*\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Configuration inheritance\n\n| Key | Inheritance rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| `intent.skills` | Uses the nearest non-null declaration between the current directory and the workspace or project root. A nearer declaration replaces its parent; omitted or null values inherit. |\n| `intent.exclude` | Combines arrays from the root through the current directory, then adds excludes passed by the caller. |\n\n## `intent.skills`\n\n`intent.skills` is a package-source and skill allowlist. A permitted package or skill can:\n\n- Appear in `list` and `stale`.\n- Resolve through `load`.\n- Contribute mappings to `install --map`.\n\nDefault `install` helps configure permissions on first use. See [Existing projects](#existing-projects) for how it handles saved or inherited configuration, and [Trust model](./trust-model) for the trust boundaries.\n\nPackage selectors permit current and future skills in the package. Exact selectors use `<package>#<skill>` and permit only that skill. If both match, the package selector takes precedence. `intent.exclude` is applied afterward and can still block either choice.\n\n### Source entries\n\nEach array entry names one source:\n\n| Entry | Kind | Meaning |\n| ----- | ---- | ------- |\n| `@scope/pkg` or `pkg` | npm | An npm package reachable through the dependency tree, direct or transitive. |\n| `@scope/pkg#skill` | npm | One exact skill in an npm package. |\n| `workspace:@scope/pkg` | workspace | A package in the current workspace. |\n| `workspace:@scope/pkg#skill` | workspace | One exact skill in a workspace package. |\n| `@scope/*` | npm | Every discovered npm package whose name matches the pattern. |\n| `workspace:@scope/*` | workspace | Every discovered workspace package whose name matches the pattern. |\n| `git:<host>/<repo>#<ref>` | git | Reserved. Not yet supported, and rejected until a future version adds it. |\n\n#### Validation rules\n\n- Exact selectors require a non-empty package name and a non-empty skill name without wildcards.\n- Package patterns support `*`, including scoped patterns such as `@tanstack/*`. Patterns cannot be combined with an exact skill selector.\n- Source kinds must match: bare selectors permit npm sources; `workspace:` selectors permit workspace sources.\n- `git:` entries are rejected, including entries containing `#` for a Git ref.\n\nA malformed entry fails the whole command. Intent reports every bad entry at once.\n\n### Special forms\n\n| Form | Result | Notice |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Absent:** no effective `intent.skills` key | Discovery commands surface every discovered package as migration behavior. | Deprecation notice until you configure permissions. |\n| **Empty:** `\"skills\": []` | Surfaces no packages. | Info notice on stderr. |\n| **Wildcard:** `\"skills\": [\"*\"]` | Permits every discovered package across scopes and source kinds, broader than `@tanstack/*`. | Acknowledged-risk notice: unvetted skills may reach your agent. |\n\nAll policy notices go to stderr. Exclusions still apply to these forms.\n\n#### Discovery notices\n\n| Situation | Notice |\n| --- | --- |\n| Discovered package is not permitted | Human output names omitted packages in one notice. Agent sessions receive only hidden package and skill counts. |\n| Configured package was not discovered | Reports that the package was not discovered. |\n| Configured exact skill is not in its discovered package | Reports that the entry was not discovered. |\n| Package was explicitly excluded | No unlisted-source notice. |\n\n### Existing projects\n\nRun `intent list` to see which packages the current policy surfaces.\n\n| Current configuration | Default `intent install` behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Saved or inherited `intent.skills` | Updates guidance only. Keeps permissions unchanged and does not prompt. |\n| No effective `intent.skills` | Starts interactive permission setup. Non-TTY execution fails without writes. |\n\nFirst-run setup offers **Enable all**, **Choose packages or scopes**, and **Choose individual skills**, followed by one confirmation before saving to the nearest owning `package.json` and installing guidance.\n\n- **Compact rules:** Enable all saves `\"*\"`; package choices save names such as `\"@tanstack/ai\"`; explicit scope choices save patterns such as `\"@tanstack/*\"`. These rules include future matching skills and packages. Individual choices save exact names such as `\"@tanstack/ai#skill\"`.\n- **Optional skill review:** choose **Review individual skills** at confirmation, then pick which selected packages to inspect. Leave the list empty to keep all selected skills. Only those packages open individual skill lists; unchecking a skill covered by a broad rule adds an exclusion. Existing and inherited exclusions stay in force.\n- **Changing instructions:** access choices do not record approval of specific content. Skills can change with dependency updates; update notifications are not available yet.\n- **Empty selection:** explicitly confirms disabling all skills with `[]`. Empty or fully excluded discovery writes nothing, so setup can be retried.\n\nFor example, enabling a scope and unchecking one skill saves:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"skills\": [\"@tanstack/*\"],\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/ai#skill\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis permits matching npm packages, including future additions, except the excluded skill. Selecting several packages individually never silently expands to a scope rule.\n\nSee [Default install](../cli/intent-install#default-install) for picker controls and cancellation behavior.\n\n### Suppressing notices temporarily\n\nUse `--no-notices` to suppress non-critical notices on stderr for one run:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest list --no-notices\n@tanstack/intent@latest install --map --no-notices\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nFor CI or wrapper scripts, set `INTENT_NO_NOTICES=1` to suppress notices without changing command arguments.\n\nDiscovery and resolution warnings are separate from policy notices and are not suppressed by these options. The acknowledged-risk notice for `\"skills\": [\"*\"]` also remains visible when other notices are suppressed.\n\n## `intent.exclude`\n\n`intent.exclude` removes packages or individual skills after the allowlist resolves.\n\nUse `intent exclude` to manage this list from the CLI:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest exclude add @tanstack/router#experimental-*\n@tanstack/intent@latest exclude remove @tanstack/router#experimental-*\n@tanstack/intent@latest exclude list\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/*devtools*\", \"@tanstack/router#experimental-*\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Exclusion patterns\n\n| Pattern | Excludes |\n| --- | --- |\n| `@scope/pkg` | The whole package. |\n| `@scope/pkg#search-params` | One named skill. |\n| `@scope/pkg#experimental-*` | Matching skills in one package. |\n| `*#experimental-*` | Matching skills across packages. |\n| `@scope/pkg#*` | The whole package, using the `#*` shortcut. |\n\nEach segment supports exact names and `*` wildcards only. Excludes apply to both npm and workspace sources with matching names, regardless of source kind.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Configuration\nid: configuration\n---\n\nConfigure Intent in the `intent` object in `package.json`:\n\n- **`skills`** permits packages or individual skills.\n- **`exclude`** blocks packages or skills after permissions are evaluated.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"skills\": [\n      \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"@acme/*\",\n      \"@tanstack/start#routing\",\n      \"workspace:@scope/internal\"\n    ],\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/router#experimental-*\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Configuration inheritance\n\n| Key | Inheritance rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| `intent.skills` | Uses the nearest non-null declaration between the current directory and the workspace or project root. A nearer declaration replaces its parent; omitted or null values inherit. |\n| `intent.exclude` | Combines arrays from the root through the current directory, then adds excludes passed by the caller. |\n\n## `intent.skills`\n\n`intent.skills` is a package-source and skill allowlist. A permitted package or skill can:\n\n- Appear in `list` and `stale`.\n- Resolve through `load`.\n- Contribute mappings to `install --map`.\n\nDefault `install` helps configure permissions on first use. See [Existing projects](#existing-projects) for how it handles saved or inherited configuration, and [Trust model](./trust-model) for the trust boundaries.\n\nPackage selectors permit current and future skills in the package. Exact selectors use `<package>#<skill>` and permit only that skill. If both match, the package selector takes precedence. `intent.exclude` is applied afterward and can still block either choice.\n\n### Source entries\n\nEach array entry names one source:\n\n| Entry | Kind | Meaning |\n| ----- | ---- | ------- |\n| `@scope/pkg` or `pkg` | npm | An npm package reachable through the dependency tree, direct or transitive. |\n| `@scope/pkg#skill` | npm | One exact skill in an npm package. |\n| `workspace:@scope/pkg` | workspace | A package in the current workspace. |\n| `workspace:@scope/pkg#skill` | workspace | One exact skill in a workspace package. |\n| `@scope/*` | npm | Every discovered npm package whose name matches the pattern. |\n| `workspace:@scope/*` | workspace | Every discovered workspace package whose name matches the pattern. |\n| `git:<host>/<repo>#<ref>` | git | Reserved. Not yet supported, and rejected until a future version adds it. |\n\n#### Validation rules\n\n- Exact selectors require a non-empty package name and a non-empty skill name without wildcards.\n- Package patterns support `*`, including scoped patterns such as `@tanstack/*`. Patterns cannot be combined with an exact skill selector.\n- Source kinds must match: bare selectors permit npm sources; `workspace:` selectors permit workspace sources.\n- `git:` entries are rejected, including entries containing `#` for a Git ref.\n\nA malformed entry fails the whole command. Intent reports every bad entry at once.\n\n### Special forms\n\n| Form | Result | Notice |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Absent:** no effective `intent.skills` key | Discovery commands surface every discovered package as migration behavior. | Deprecation notice until you configure permissions. |\n| **Empty:** `\"skills\": []` | Surfaces no packages. | Info notice on stderr. |\n| **Wildcard:** `\"skills\": [\"*\"]` | Permits every discovered package across scopes and source kinds, broader than `@tanstack/*`. | Acknowledged-risk notice: unvetted skills may reach your agent. |\n\nAll policy notices go to stderr. Exclusions still apply to these forms.\n\n#### Discovery notices\n\n| Situation | Notice |\n| --- | --- |\n| Discovered package is not permitted | Human output names omitted packages in one notice. Agent sessions receive only hidden package and skill counts. |\n| Configured package was not discovered | Reports that the package was not discovered. |\n| Configured exact skill is not in its discovered package | Reports that the entry was not discovered. |\n| Package was explicitly excluded | No unlisted-source notice. |\n\n### Existing projects\n\nRun `intent list` to see which packages the current policy surfaces.\n\n| Current configuration | Default `intent install` behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Saved or inherited `intent.skills` | Updates guidance only. Keeps permissions unchanged and does not prompt. |\n| No effective `intent.skills` | Starts interactive permission setup. Non-TTY execution fails without writes. |\n\nFirst-run setup offers **Enable all**, **Choose packages or scopes**, and **Choose individual skills**, followed by one confirmation before saving to the nearest owning `package.json` and installing guidance.\n\n- **Compact rules:** Enable all saves `\"*\"`; package choices save names such as `\"@tanstack/ai\"`; explicit scope choices save patterns such as `\"@tanstack/*\"`. These rules include future matching skills and packages. Individual choices save exact names such as `\"@tanstack/ai#skill\"`.\n- **Optional skill review:** choose **Review individual skills** at confirmation, then pick which selected packages to inspect. Leave the list empty to keep all selected skills. Only those packages open individual skill lists; unchecking a skill covered by a broad rule adds an exclusion. Existing and inherited exclusions stay in force.\n- **Changing instructions:** access choices do not record approval of specific content. Skills can change with dependency updates; update notifications are not available yet.\n- **Empty selection:** explicitly confirms disabling all skills with `[]`. Empty or fully excluded discovery writes nothing, so setup can be retried.\n\nFor example, enabling a scope and unchecking one skill saves:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"skills\": [\"@tanstack/*\"],\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/ai#skill\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis permits matching npm packages, including future additions, except the excluded skill. Selecting several packages individually never silently expands to a scope rule.\n\nSee [Default install](../cli/intent-install#default-install) for picker controls and cancellation behavior.\n\n### Suppressing notices temporarily\n\nUse `--no-notices` to suppress non-critical notices on stderr for one run:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest list --no-notices\n@tanstack/intent@latest install --map --no-notices\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nFor CI or wrapper scripts, set `INTENT_NO_NOTICES=1` to suppress notices without changing command arguments.\n\nDiscovery and resolution warnings are separate from policy notices and are not suppressed by these options. The acknowledged-risk notice for `\"skills\": [\"*\"]` also remains visible when other notices are suppressed.\n\n## `intent.exclude`\n\n`intent.exclude` removes packages or individual skills after the allowlist resolves.\n\nUse `intent exclude` to manage this list from the CLI:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest exclude add @tanstack/router#experimental-*\n@tanstack/intent@latest exclude remove @tanstack/router#experimental-*\n@tanstack/intent@latest exclude list\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```json\n{\n  \"intent\": {\n    \"exclude\": [\"@tanstack/*devtools*\", \"@tanstack/router#experimental-*\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Exclusion patterns\n\n| Pattern | Excludes |\n| --- | --- |\n| `@scope/pkg` | The whole package. |\n| `@scope/pkg#search-params` | One named skill. |\n| `@scope/pkg#experimental-*` | Matching skills in one package. |\n| `*#experimental-*` | Matching skills across packages. |\n| `@scope/pkg#*` | The whole package, using the `#*` shortcut. |\n\nEach segment supports exact names and `*` wildcards only. Excludes apply to both npm and workspace sources with matching names, regardless of source kind.\n"}
